#. Tag: title
#: quanta-projects.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid "New Projects"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &quantaplus; project wizard (<menuchoice> <guimenu>Project</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>New Project...</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>) makes project "
"creation an easy task."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Project Wizard."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The fields are pretty straight forward. It is best to fill them in from top "
"to bottom. Filling in a project name will autocomplete all the folder "
"structure for the rest of the project. All of the paths and author "
"information fields can be configured later on clicking <menuchoice> "
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Shift;<keycap>F7</keycap></keycombo> "
"</shortcut> <guimenu>Project</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Project Properties</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: quanta-projects.docbook:80 quanta-projects.docbook:408
#, no-c-format
msgid "General Project Settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid "Name"
msgstr "Nom"

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you fill in the name for your project. For example, we will call ours "
"<quote><literal>foo</literal>.</quote> When you fill in <guilabel>Name</"
"guilabel>, <guilabel>File</guilabel> is filled out for you automatically."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "File"
msgstr "Fichièr"

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the name of the &quantaplus; project file. By default, it is the "
"name of your project, but in lowercase letters and without spaces. It uses "
"the extension <literal role=\"extension\">webprj</literal> (&eg; "
"<filename>foo.webprj</filename>). This file is stored in the root of the "
"project's Main Folder."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: quanta-projects.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid "Server Settings"
msgstr "Paramètres del servidor"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:113 quanta-projects.docbook:709
#, no-c-format
msgid "Protocol"
msgstr "Protocòl"

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you select the protocol you will be using to access you project. If "
"your project is on the same machine that you are using Quanta Plus on, then "
"leave the value at Local. The list of protocols shown here is dependant of "
"your system setup. Available protocols include SSH, FTP, NFS, SMB, WebDAV, "
"and others. The protocol list is powered by &kde;'s powerful KIOSlave "
"architecture. This framework allows every &kde; application to easily access "
"remote information as if it is local to the machine."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:128 quanta-projects.docbook:699
#, no-c-format
msgid "Host"
msgstr "Òste"

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you fill in the server address of the machine you want to access, "
"unless you are working through the Local protocol. Either a hostname "
"(hostname.example.com) or an IP address (127.0.0.1) can go here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:138 quanta-projects.docbook:731
#, no-c-format
msgid "User"
msgstr "Utilizaire"

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid "User name for logging onto the remote machine. This is case-sensitive."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:146 quanta-projects.docbook:740
#, no-c-format
msgid "Password"
msgstr "Mot de pas"

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "Password for logging onto the remote machine. This is case-sensitive."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:154 quanta-projects.docbook:720
#, no-c-format
msgid "Port"
msgstr "Pòrt"

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Leave this field blank to use the default port for the protocol you are "
"using. You may need to change this depending on your server's configuration."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: quanta-projects.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid "Directory Settings"
msgstr "Paramètres dels repertòris"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid "Main directory"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the root folder where all of the project files and folders will be "
"stored."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid "Templates directory"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is where the templates for this project will be stored. It is a "
"relative path to the project and by default, it points to <filename class="
"\"directory\">templates</filename>. If you have a common set of files that "
"you use for several projects, then it may be useful to point this field to "
"it, instead of to the default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:197
#, no-c-format
msgid "Toolbars directory"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is where the toolbars for this project will be stored. It is a relative "
"path to the project and by default, it points to <filename>toolbars</"
"filename>. If you have a common set of toolbars that you use for several "
"projects, it may be useful to point this there instead of the default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: quanta-projects.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid "Project Sources"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:220
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add local or remote files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This allows you to get files from the local file system. You can choose "
"multiple files or entire folders."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use wget to download files from site"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option is great if you have static web content that you wish to "
"download and modify. For server side scripting (&eg; &PHP;, Python, &etc;.) "
"you will have to get the files another way."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: quanta-projects.docbook:244
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert Files in Project"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert file from"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Check this if you wish to include files found in the path of the Main "
"Folder. Leave unchecked when starting a project from scratch."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: quanta-projects.docbook:255
#, no-c-format
msgid "Filters"
msgstr "Filtres"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert only markup, script and image files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choosing this option will only insert markup, script, and image files into "
"your project."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:268
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert files with the following mask"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:270
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choosing this option will display all files and folders within the Main "
"Folder and allow you to be more specific with your choices."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:280
#, no-c-format
msgid "Included files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This displays a list of the files in the Main Folder. You can choose the "
"desired files for inclusion, by checking, or exclusion, by unchecking, in "
"your project."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: quanta-projects.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid "More Project Settings"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:294
#, no-c-format
msgid "Author"
msgstr "Autor"

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert your name (or alias) here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid "Email"
msgstr "Adreça electronica"

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:304
#, no-c-format
msgid "The address where you would like email regarding this project to go."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: quanta-projects.docbook:310
#, no-c-format
msgid "Project Defaults"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid "Default DTD"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:316
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose the markup language you will be working with the most within this "
"project."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:323
#, no-c-format
msgid "Default encoding"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:325
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose the character encoding you wish the files in your project to be "
"opened and saved with."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use preview prefix"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Check this to use a prefix for your previews. This allows you to set the "
"path prefix to something other than your local file system. This is most "
"useful for pages that contain dynamic content and are dependent on server "
"processing (like &PHP;, <acronym>JSS</acronym>, Python, &etc;). Simply type "
"in the first portion of the address as it exists on that server and the "
"filepath at the end will be complete by &quantaplus;. For example, if you "
"have the domain <literal>bar.com</literal> and you are editing the "
"<filename>index.html</filename> page, you could edit it on your remote "
"machine (<systemitem>foo.bar.com</systemitem>), upload it to the server and "
"press <keycap>F6</keycap> to see the results from <systemitem>www.bar.com</"
"systemitem> instead of your local file system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:352
#, no-c-format
msgid "Prefix"
msgstr "Prefixe"

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:354
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter the prefix you wish to use here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:363
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert global templates"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:365
#, no-c-format
msgid "This makes a copy of the global templates in your projects folder tree."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:371
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert local templates"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid "This makes a copy of the local templates in your projects folder tree."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:380
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The last screen of the new project wizard has 3 settings that can make your "
"life easier. These settings are available for change from the <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Project</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Project Properties</guimenuitem> </"
"menuchoice> menu tree on the Upload Profiles Tab or with the keyboard "
"shortcut <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Shift;<keycap>F7</keycap></keycombo>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: quanta-projects.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring Projects"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:395
#, no-c-format
msgid "The project properties dialog looks like:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:401
#, no-c-format
msgid "The general options page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:405
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Some of the items are the same as in the project wizard and are described in "
"<xref linkend=\"create-new-project-3-2\"/>. The extra items are described "
"below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:410
#, no-c-format
msgid "Exclude from project"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:412
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A list of file names (wildcards can be used) that will be ignored when you "
"do project related operations like <guimenuitem>Rescan Project Folder</"
"guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:418
#, no-c-format
msgid "Exclude files listed in .cvsignore"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:420
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A complementary option to the above one, also files listed in the .cvsignore "
"file will be excluded from the project."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:426 quanta-projects.docbook:444
#, no-c-format
msgid "Default view"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:428 quanta-projects.docbook:446
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The project view that will be loaded when the project is opened. You can "
"read more about project views in <xref linkend=\"project-views-3-2\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:435
#, no-c-format
msgid "Debugger"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:437
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the debugger you want to use. Currently only Gubed is support. You "
"can find more information about Gubed at <ulink url=\"http://gubed."
"sourceforge.net\"></ulink>.The debugger plugin can be configured with the "
"<guilabel>Options</guilabel> button. read <xref linkend=\"debugging-3-2\"/> "
"to learn more about debugging."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:454
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the <guilabel>Upload Profiles</guilabel> page you can configure the "
"upload profiles (see <xref linkend=\"upload-profiles\"/>), as well as enable "
"the showing of a treeview with the content of the server for each profile by "
"checking the <guilabel>Show a treeview for each profile</guilabel> checkbox."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:456
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the <guilabel>Team Configuration</guilabel> page you can add, edit and "
"remove members of the project as well as define a mailing list. Read <xref "
"linkend=\"team-members\"/> for details."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:459
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the <guilabel>Event Configuration</guilabel> page you can "
"<guilabel>Enable the event actions</guilabel>, add, modify and remove these "
"actions. Event actions are executed when some predefined event occurs, like "
"saving a file. See <xref linkend=\"event-actions\"/> for details."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: quanta-projects.docbook:465
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using Projects"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: quanta-projects.docbook:468
#, no-c-format
msgid "Project Files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:470
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default &quantaplus; will open the last project accessed when launched. "
"This behavior is not currently configurable."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:475
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To open another project, select <guimenuitem>Open Project...</guimenuitem> "
"from the <guimenu>Project</guimenu> menu or the <guiicon>Open Project</"
"guiicon> icon on the toolbar. The open project dialog will pop up and allow "
"you to choose the project you wish. Projects have a <literal role=\"extension"
"\">webprj</literal> extension."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:483
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When closing &quantaplus;, your project file will be saved automatically. "
"You will be asked to save any changes before exiting if &quantaplus; detects "
"any changed files. This same behavior occurs if you load a new project."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: quanta-projects.docbook:493
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Project Tree View"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:495
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The project tree view gives you uncluttered access to the files in your "
"project. This is where you manage the files in the current project."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:500
#, no-c-format
msgid "For files, a &RMB; click brings up the following menu:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:508
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These items are fairly self-explanatory and will be left to the reader for "
"exploration."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:513
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Folders are similar but do not contain the <guimenuitem>Open</guimenuitem> "
"and <guimenuitem>Open With...</guimenuitem> &RMB; menu items:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:524
#, no-c-format
msgid "These items are left to the reader for exploration as well."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: quanta-projects.docbook:531
#, no-c-format
msgid "Uploading Projects"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:533
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Upload Project dialog:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:541
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Upload Project dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:546 quanta-projects.docbook:693
#, no-c-format
msgid "Profile name"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:548
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is where different <link linkend=\"upload-profiles\">profiles</link> "
"can be chosen. The profile contains information on where the uploaded files "
"are to be placed. Read <xref linkend=\"upload-profiles\"/>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: quanta-projects.docbook:555
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>New</guibutton>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:557
#, no-c-format
msgid "This button allows you to create new upload profiles."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: quanta-projects.docbook:564
#, no-c-format
msgid "Edit"
msgstr "Edicion"

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:566
#, no-c-format
msgid "This allows you to edit the currently selected upload profile."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: quanta-projects.docbook:573
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remove"
msgstr "Suprimir"

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:575
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This allows you to remove the current profile. If only one profile is "
"available the button is grayed out to prevent its removal."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:584
#, no-c-format
msgid "Keep passwords in memory"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:586
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The password is stored in memory and is lost as soon as the program is "
"closed. This option is useful if frequent uploading of files is necessary "
"and you do not want to use the more insecure <quote>Store password on disc</"
"quote> option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: quanta-projects.docbook:595
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>All</guibutton>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:597
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select all files in your project for upload."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: quanta-projects.docbook:604
#, no-c-format
msgid "Modified"
msgstr "Modificat"

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:606
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select all modified files for upload."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: quanta-projects.docbook:613
#, no-c-format
msgid "None"
msgstr "Pas cap"

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:615
#, no-c-format
msgid "Unselects all files in the list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: quanta-projects.docbook:622
#, no-c-format
msgid "Invert"
msgstr "Enversar"

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:624
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selects/Unselects all files in the list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: quanta-projects.docbook:631
#, no-c-format
msgid "Expand All"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:633
#, no-c-format
msgid "Expands all folders."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: quanta-projects.docbook:640
#, no-c-format
msgid "Collapse All"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:642
#, no-c-format
msgid "Collaspes all folders."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: quanta-projects.docbook:649
#, no-c-format
msgid "Update All"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:651
#, no-c-format
msgid "Refreshes list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: quanta-projects.docbook:658
#, no-c-format
msgid "Proceed"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:660
#, no-c-format
msgid "Start the upload"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: quanta-projects.docbook:667
#, no-c-format
msgid "Cancel"
msgstr "Anullar"

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:669
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will abort your transfer in progress or just exit out of the dialog if "
"you change your mind before starting the upload."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: quanta-projects.docbook:680
#, no-c-format
msgid "Upload profiles"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:681
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"With &quantaplus; you can define multiple upload profiles and, in this way, "
"upload your project (or parts of your project) to different servers. When "
"you edit or create a profile you will face the following dialog:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:695
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter the name you wish to give your profile here."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:701
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the hostname of the server you are copying the files to. Either a "
"fully qualified domain name, or an IP address is needed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:711
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Transfer protocol to use for this upload. Depending on your version of &kde; "
"this list will vary. At the very least you should be able to choose from "
"&FTP;, file (&ie; local) and <acronym>NFS</acronym>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:722
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Port for the transfer. Usually this will not need to be changed unless your "
"network administrator is hosting a service on a port other than its well "
"known port."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:733
#, no-c-format
msgid "Username to use for authentication."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:742
#, no-c-format
msgid "Password to use for authentication."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:749
#, no-c-format
msgid "Store password on disc"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:751
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Depending on your level of paranoia, this is a time saving feature, or a "
"danger. Use it at your discretion. The password is kept on disk as text in "
"an obscured form, so it's not simple to read it, but anyone with programming "
"knowledge can easily un-obscure it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:759
#, no-c-format
msgid "Path"
msgstr "Camin"

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:761
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the base path on the remote host that you will be copying files to."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: quanta-projects.docbook:769
#, no-c-format
msgid "Use as default profile"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:771
#, no-c-format
msgid "Allows you to mark the profile currently being viewed as the default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: quanta-projects.docbook:781
#, no-c-format
msgid "Project Views"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:782
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A project view is just a set of files and toolbars. You can have multiple "
"views in a project, meaning that by simply changing the view you can load "
"several files and toolbars which will replace the currently opened files and "
"toolbars."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:785
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Views can be saved, opened, deleted using the <guimenu>Project</guimenu> "
"menu or the <guilabel>Project Toolbar</guilabel>, accessible via "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guisubmenu>Toolbars</"
"guisubmenu><guimenuitem>Project Toolbar</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: quanta-projects.docbook:788
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can have a default view (loaded when the project is opened). See <xref "
"linkend=\"configuring-projects-3-2\"/>."
msgstr ""
